# A checked degree-160 orbit-basis inverse

The two arrays transcribe `left_basis` and `left_inverse` in the saved ATLAS
J2G1-f2r160B0 rank-one discovery record, using bit j for column j. The kernel
checks their product, then the canonical map from ZMod 2 transports that
identity to every characteristic-two field. This is the left-inverse premise
of `LargeModels.top_of_rankOne` for that candidate. The remaining generator,
rank-one and orbit identities are independent construction obligations.

Generated by `source/generate_basis160.py`; attribution and original sources
are preserved in `source/README.md`. No GAP answer is a proof premise.
-/

